      "scene": "INT. ELEVEN’S ROOM - NIGHT",
      "speech_type": "direct",
      "dialogue": "I am -- a monster. DR. BRENNER You speak of monsters... of superheroes. Those are the stuff of myth and fairy tales, Eleven. Reality -- truth -- is rarely so simple. People are not so easily defined. 77.. DDRR.. BBRREENNNNEERR ((CCOONNTT’’DD)) Only by facing all of ourselves -- the good and the bad -- can we become whole."
    },
    {
      "scene": "INT. ELEVEN’S ROOM - NIGHT",
      "speech_type": "direct",
      "dialogue": "What if -- I don’t want to become... whole? DR. BRENNER Then that is a choice. Your choice. The door is always open, Eleven. This place -- is not a prison. DR. BRENNER This is. DR. BRENNER You chose to trust me once. And now I am asking you trust me again. Journey with me into the past. One last time. No more hiding, Eleven."
    },
